 my experiments. Psychoanalysis as thesis -- Brain science as antithesis -- Cognitive neuroscience as synthesis -- [pt.] IV. Experiments of nature. Brain shock -- Brain death -- Heart failure -- Back ache -- Sleep strangulation -- [pt.] V. Implications of my work. Philosophical implications -- Scientific implications -- Dream science and the humanities -- Functional conclusions.","note":[{"@type":"statement of responsibility","#text":"J. Allan Hobson."},{"@type":"bibliography","#text":"Includes bibliographical references (pages 281-291) and index."}],"subject":[{"@authority":"lcsh","name":{"@type":"personal","namePart":["Hobson, J. Allan",{"@type":"date","#text":"1933-"}]}},{"@authority":"mesh","name":{"@type":"personal","namePart":["Hobson, J. Allan",{"@type":"date","#text":"1933-"}]}},{"@authority":"fast","name":{"@type":"personal","namePart":["Hobson, J. Allan",{"@type":"date","#text":"1933-"}]}},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":"Neuroscientists","genre":"Biography"},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":"Dreams"},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":"Dream interpretation"},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":"Rapid eye movement sleep"},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":"Consciousness"},{"@authority":"bisacsh","topic":["HEALTH & FITNESS","Diseases","Nervous System (incl. Brain)"]},{"@authority":"bisacsh","topic":["MEDICAL","Neurology"]},{"@authority":"bisacsh","topic":["BIOGRAPHY & AUTOBIOGRAPHY","Medical"]},{"@authority":"fast","topic":"Consciousness"},{"@authority":"fast","topic":"Dream interpretation"},{"@authority":"fast","topic":"Dreams"},{"@authority":"fast","topic":"Neuroscientists"},{"@authority":"fast","topic":"Rapid eye movement sleep"},{"topic":"COGNITIVE SCIENCES/Psychology/Cognitive Psychology"},{"topic":"NEUROSCIENCE/General"},{"topic":"COGNITIVE SCIENCES/General"}],"classification":[{"@authority":"lcc","#text":"QP353.4.H63 A3 2011eb"},{"@edition":"22","@authority":"ddc","#text":"616.80092"}],"relatedItem":[{"@type":"otherFormat","@otherType":"Print version:","@displayLabel":"Print version:","titleInfo":{"title":"Dream life"},"name":{"namePart":"Hobson, J. Allan, 1933-"},"originInfo":{"publisher":"Cambridge, Mass. : MIT Press, ©2011"},"identifier":[{"@type":"local","#text":"(DLC)  2010030562"},{"@type":"local","#text":"(OCoLC)711315286"}]},{"@otherType":"HOLLIS record","location":{"url":"https://id.lib.harvard.edu/alma/99154300368203941/catalog"}}],"identifier":[{"@type":"isbn","#text":"9780262295598"},{"@type":"isbn","#text":"0262295598"},{"@type":"isbn","#text":"1283119145"},{"@type":"isbn","#text":"9781283119146"},{"@type":"isbn","@invalid":"yes","#text":"9780262015325"},{"@type":"isbn","@invalid":"yes","#text":"0262015323"},{"@type":"oclc","#text":"727944957"},{"@type":"oclc","#text":"ocn727944957"},{"@type":"stock number","#text":"8633 MIT Press"},{"@type":"stock number","#text":"9780262295598 MIT Press"}],"location":[null,null],"extension":[{"librarycloud":{"originalDocument":"https://s3.amazonaws.com/harvard.librarycloud.marc/99154300368203941","processingDate":"2021-01-23T21:48Z"}},{"sets":null}],"recordInfo":{"descriptionStandard":["aacr","pn"],"recordContentSource":{"@authority":"marcorg","#text":"N$T"},"recordCreationDate":{"@encoding":"marc","#text":"110601"},"recordChangeDate":{"@encoding":"iso8601","#text":"20200602"},"recordIdentifier":{"@source":"MH:ALMA","#text":"99154300368203941"},"recordOrigin":"Converted from MARCXML to MODS version 3.6 using MARC21slim2MODS3-6.xsl\n        (Revision 1.117 2017/02/14)","languageOfCataloging":{"languageTerm":{"@type":"code","@authority":"iso639-2b","#text":"eng"}}}},{"titleInfo":[{"title":"13 dreams Freud never had","subTitle":"the new mind science"},{"@type":"alternative","title":"Thirteen dreams Freud never had"}],"name":{"@usage":"primary","@type":"personal","namePart":["Hobson, J. Allan",{"@type":"date","#text":"1933-"}],"role":{"roleTerm":{"@type":"text","#text":"creator"}}},"typeOfResource":"text","genre":{"@authority":"marcgt","#text":"bibliography"},"originInfo":{"place":[{"placeTerm":[{"@type":"code","@authority":"marccountry","#text":"nyu"},{"@type":"text","@authority":"marccountry","#text":"New York (State)"}]},{"placeTerm":{"@type":"text","#text":"New York"}}],"publisher":"Pi","dateIssued":["c2005",{"@encoding":"marc","#text":"2005"}],"issuance":"monographic"},"language":{"languageTerm":[{"@type":"code","@authority":"iso639-2b","#text":"eng"},{"@type":"text","@authority":"iso639-2b","#text":"English"}]},"physicalDescription":{"form":{"@authority":"marcform","#text":"print"},"extent":"xx, 204 p. : ill. ; 22 cm."},"abstract":{"@type":"Review","#text":"\"Freud believed dreams resulted from an elaborate effort of the mind to conceal unacceptable instinctual wishes welling up from the unconscious when the ego relaxes its prohibition of the id in sleep. But modern neuroscience, including Hobson's own research, has shown this understanding of the brain to be wrong. As Hobson explains, the bizarre nature of our dreams has nothing to do with repressed emotion as Freud taught; it results from the way the brain is physically built. Chemical mechanisms in the brain stem during deep REM sleep, which shift the activation of various regions of the cortex, generate these changes. Here is a clear window on how thoughts are actually created from our memories of experiences.\"--Jacket."},"tableOfContents":"Dreamstage with elephants : REM sleep and creativity -- HMS marathon : turning on the social brain -- Lobster brain : the visual brain as image synthesizer -- Caravaggio : running the pons motor pattern generator -- Italian romance : playing hide-and-seek with dopamine -- Ed Evarts and Mickey Mantle : scrambling the hippocampus -- Bicentennial wine tasting : the brain gets high on its own juices -- Dangerous diving : the surprising importance of the vestibular system -- Split whale : fear and the amygdala -- Tiffany box : toward a new philosophy of mind -- Louis Kane dies : the brain plays tricks with memory -- Medieval town : bizarre architecture, emotional salience, and the healing medulla -- French kiss : the erotic hypothalamus.","targetAudience":{"@authority":"marctarget","#text":"specialized"},"note":[{"@type":"statement of responsibility","#text":"J. Allan Hobson."},{"@type":"bibliography","#text":"Includes bibliographical references (p. [181]-193) and index."}],"subject":[{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":"Brain"},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":"Cognitive psychology"},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":"Dreams"},{"@authority":"mesh","topic":"Brain"},{"@authority":"mesh","topic":"Dreams"}],"classification":[{"@authority":"lcc","#text":"QP426 .H63 2005"},{"@edition":"22","@authority":"ddc","#text":"612.82"}],"relatedItem":[{"@type":"otherFormat","@otherType":"Online version:","@displayLabel":"Online version:","titleInfo":{"title":"13 dreams Freud never had"},"name":{"namePart":"Hobson, J. Allan, 1933-"},"originInfo":{"publisher":"New York : Pi, ©2005"},"identifier":{"@type":"local","#text":"(OCoLC)638860561"}},{"@otherType":"HOLLIS record","location":{"url":"https://id.lib.harvard.edu/alma/990095175290203941/catalog"}}],"identifier":[{"@type":"isbn","#text":"0131472259 (hbk.)"},{"@type":"oclc","#text":"56652289"}],"location":[{"physicalLocation":{"@displayLabel":"Harvard repository","@type":"repository","@valueURI":"http://id.loc.gov/rwo/agents/no2014094889","#text":"Widener Library, Harvard University"},"shelfLocator":"QP426 .H615 2005x"},null,null],"extension":[{"librarycloud":{"HarvardRepositories":{"HarvardRepository":"Widener"},"originalDocument":"https://s3.amazonaws.com/harvard.librarycloud.marc/990095175290203941","priorrecordids":{"recordIdentifier":{"@source":"MH:ALEPH","#text":"009517529"}},"processingDate":"2022-12-29T09:13Z"}},{"sets":null}],"recordInfo":{"descriptionStandard":"aacr","recordContentSource":{"@authority":"marcorg","#text":"UKM"},"recordCreationDate":{"@encoding":"marc","#text":"040910"},"recordChangeDate":{"@encoding":"iso8601","#text":"20041213"},"recordIdentifier":{"@source":"MH:ALMA","#text":